<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28004" root="عته" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَتَاهِيَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَتَاهَةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>Foolish,</i> or <i>stupid:</i>
and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُتَاهِيَةٌ</span></b> ; (Akh, S, K, TA;) applied to a
man. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And, in a pl. sense, The <i>erring</i>
of mankind; and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَتَاهَةٌ</span></b> ; (K, TA;) which

latter signifies also, in a pl. sense, <i>foolish,</i> or
<i>stupid.</i> (TA.)

